  "details": "JeecgBoot through 3.9.5 contains a missing authorization vulnerability that allows low-privileged authenticated users to modify message push records by calling PUT /sys/message/sysMessage/edit. Attackers can submit a request body naming any sys_sms record id to overwrite its title, content, receiver address and send status without ownership checks.",
